      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "The vector $a$ has magnitude $7,$ the vector $b$ has magnitude $3,$ the angle between $a$ and $b$ is ${55}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $a\\times b.$ Find $a\\times b$ in terms of $n.$ Round your final answer to the nearest integer where appropriate.",
      "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|a|\\cdot |b|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =7\\cdot 3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =21(0.819…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(17.202…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈17n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
